⍝ 11 · Using the shared library (lib/Lib.apln) instead of rewriting helpers
⍝ Run:  dyalog sample-scripts/11-using-lib.apls
⍝ The `dyalog` command mounts lib/ at /apl-lib, so this line works from any folder:
⎕FIX'file:///apl-lib/Lib.apln'
S←Lib.Str ⋄ N←Lib.Stats                  ⍝ short names for the parts you use

⍝ Words in poem.txt, using Str and Sys
text←Lib.Sys.ReadText (Lib.Sys.ScriptDir⍬),'poem.txt'
words←S.Lower¨S.Words text
⎕←'words: ',(⍕≢words),'   longest: ',⊃words[⊃⍒≢¨words]

⍝ Statistics on the word lengths
len←≢¨words
⎕←'mean length:   ',⍕2 N.Round N.Mean len
⎕←'median length: ',⍕N.Median len
⎕←'most common:   ',⍕N.Mode len

⍝ A record, as JSON
r←'file' 'words' 'when' Lib.Data.Record 'poem.txt'(≢words)(Lib.Sys.Now⍬)
⎕←Lib.Data.ToJSON r
⎕←', ' S.Join Lib.Data.Fields r
